Marking
-------

Files carrying Spider content should say so in themselves, so a licence scanner reaches
the same conclusion this file does without reading prose:

  * a source file that quotes Spider content carries, near its existing licence header,
        SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2018 Yu et al., Spider 1.0 contributors
        SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 AND CC-BY-SA-4.0
  * a data file that cannot carry a comment is declared in the nearest REUSE.toml, or in
    a sidecar <filename>.license beside it.

Everything under spider/ is declared in spider/REUSE.toml. Every file outside spider/ that
quotes Spider rows carries the two lines above in itself: the calibration cases, build.py,
spider/build_slice.py, the tests, and docs/dataset.md. Anything that starts quoting a row
later is expected to be marked in the same commit that adds the quotation.


